+## Singleton-row canonical repair (2026-10-24)
+
+The retained audit was reproduced: canonical train input 0 contains a row with
+one nonzero marker, the Racket authority emits one cyan cell, and version 1.1.1
+rejected that row while normal generation never emitted it. Version 1.2.0 now
+accepts singleton active rows, exposes `row_profile=singleton_mixed`, and emits
+exactly one singleton alongside ordinary separated spans in that profile. A
+Python rule mirror, the exact canonical `RULE_HASH`, and strict ARC-cell
+validation were added.
+
+`tests/test_singleton_rows.py` covers every canonical singleton-bearing pair,
+a generated mixed witness, the “ignore singleton rows” rival, protected-Racket
+parity, and bool/out-of-range/non-integer rejection. The bounded 128-draw probe
+saw both normal profiles (60 span-only, 68 mixed), no self-check failures, and a
+one-cell disagreement between the retained rival and the Racket label. The
+broader legacy palette/texture/axis contract was not audited or repaired here;
+owner approval remains pending.
